    "media:imagetext": "ARRIVAL OF THE \"CHINA CLIPPER\"\n5½ DAYS OUT OF THE ORIENT\nAfter a 9,000 mile Trans-Pacific sky voyage\nof three\n\"Clipper\" Ships,\n\"Hawaii\"\nand \"Philippine\"\nups Deween Caltom and the Orient by Fan-\nAmerican Airways System.\nStops are made\nat the Hawaiian, Midway, Wake, Guam, and\nPhilippine Islands, en\nroute, reducing a\nmonth's sea voyage to five\nand one-half\ndays.\nThese ships are capable of carrying a\nton of mail and\nexpress-will accommodate\nforty seated or eighteen sleeping passengers\non a normal flight. The ships have a\n: fuel\ncapacity for a flight of 3,000 miles, with a\nhigh speed of 180 miles per hour.\nPictorial Wonderland\nPLACE\nONE CENT\nSTAMP\nHERE\nSTANLEY A. PILTZ\nCOMPANY, SAN\nFRANCISCO, CALIF•\nPOST CARD\nA AS\n35\n2018121297",
